WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.583
Open the Office page and choose Full reinstall.

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:11.417
Unlike installation alone, it first removes existing Office and then deploys it again using the installation
configuration.

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:16.292
Save your documents, back up settings you need to keep and read the notice.

00:00:16.292 --> 00:00:19.917
Full reinstall is not a simple repair button.

00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:24.417
Confirm that you accept removing the existing Office installation.

00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:29.042
Choose PowerShell or CMD to match your administrator terminal.

00:00:29.042 --> 00:00:32.167
The website only provides a command.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:36.167
Selecting Full reinstall does not start uninstalling.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:40.500
Click Copy full command or download and copy the text.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.083
Keep every part, because it includes configuration download and verification checks before removal.

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:51.667
Paste and review the command, then decide whether to execute it.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.417
This scene is an illustration.

00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:59.875
It does not uninstall or install software and does not invent a successful result.

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:08.167
If configuration cannot download, returns 403 or fails verification, the script stops before uninstalling.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.042
Do not skip preflight checks.

00:01:11.042 --> 00:01:16.125
Check reinstall results and licensing separately using the actual output.
